  "raw_text": "109\n\nKlir kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto see clearly\n \n/ ver claramente\n\nKlir marikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto show clearly, to emphasize\n \n/ mostrar claramente, enfatizar\n\nSmalkanka yamnika nani ba klir marikaia\n \n(\nth-13-tit\n)\n \n–\n \nPractical Value Made Clear\n \n/ Resaltar el valor\npráctico\n\nSmalkanka tânka tara nani ba klir mariks\n \n(\nth-14-tit\n)\n \n–\n \nMain Points Made to Stand Out\n \n/ Destacar los\npuntos principales\n\nKlir sakaia\n \n(\ndict\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto be free from something\n \n/ ser liberado de algo\n\nKlir takaia\n \n(\ndict\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto be cleared, to be free of\n \n/ ser despejado, estar libre de\n\nKlir wiaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto say clearly\n \n/ decir claramente\n\nKlisang\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nreed-grass\n \n/ caña\n\nKlua\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \numbilical cord\n \n/ cordón umbilical\n\n(Construct:\n \nKlui\n;\n \nKluam\n;\n \nAi klua\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nvop\n):\n \nBâra yang klui bikan\n \n–\n \nThere my umbilical cord is buried\n \n/ Allí está enterrado mi cordón umbilical)\n\nKlubaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto embrace, to hug, to gather things together in the arms, to flirt\n \n/ abrazar, juntar cosas en los brazos,\ncoquetear\n\nKlubanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsomething gathered together in the arms,\n \narmful,\n \nbunch\n \n/ algo juntado en los brazos,\n \nalgo\n\namontonado en los brazos o las manos\n\nKlubi alkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto embrace, to hug\n \n/ abrazar\n \n(See also/\n \nV\ner también:\n \nKiaubi alkaia\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nbh68\n):\n \nLasarus ra rait karna klubi alkan kaia sa\n \n–\n \n(They) must\n \nhave given Lasarus a really big embrace\n \n/ (Ellos) deben\n\nhaber dado a Lasarus un abrazo realmente grande\n)\n\nKlukum\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npato\n \n/ duck\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \ndb\n-\nKli Smalkanka 14:16\n \nuses\n \nKlukum\n \ns\nȃ\ntka wala\n \nto translate “swan” /\n \ndb\n-\nKli Smalkanka 14:16\n \nusa\n \nKlukum\n \ns\nȃ\ntka wala\n\npara traducir “cisne”)\n\nKlungbaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nKlunhbaia\n)\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nKlungwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto bruise, to contuse, to cut, to peel\n \n/ magullar, contusionar,\ncortar, pelar\n \nSee how this is commonly used in speech\n\nKlungka\n \n(a/t:\n \nKluhngka\n-dict\n;\n \nKlunhka\n-dictu-alt\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nstomach\n \n/ estomago\n\nKlungwaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nKlunhwaia\n)\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nKlungbaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto be bruised, to be contused, to be cut, to be peeled\n \n/ ser\nmagullado, contundente, ser cortado, ser pelado\n \nCommonly used?\n\nTaya klungwan\n \n(a/t:\n \nTaya klunhwan\n) (\ndb-Isa53:5\n)\n \n–\n \nflayed skin, cut skin, torn skin\n \n/ piel desollada, piel cortada,\npiel rasgada\n\nKlutka\n \n(a/t:\n \nKluntka\n)\n \n–\n \nshort (length of time or distance)\n \n/ corto (cantidad de tiempo of distancia)\n \n(See also/ Ver\ntambién:\n \nKunhku\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nKlutka aisamna\n \n–\n \nI will speak briefly\n \n/ Voy a hablar brevemente)\n\nKmakmaya\n \n(\ndb,dictu,dict-alt\n;\n \nMahkmaia\n-\ndict\n;\n \nMakmaya\n-\ndictu-alt\n;\n \nMahkmaya\n-\ndictu-alt\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \njaw\n \n/ mandíbula,\nquijada\n\n(Construct (\ndict\n):\n \nMaihkmaia\n;\n \nMahmkmaia\n;\n \nMahkmaia\n)\n\nKolosi\n \n(\ndb,dba\n;\n \nKolosi Nanira\n-dbta,lrw\n)\n \n–\n \nColossians\n \n(Bible book) / Colosenses (libro bíblico)\n\nKordoba\n \n(\naem\n)\n \n–\n \ncordoba\n \n/ córdoba\n\nKorint\n \n(\ndb,dba,dbta\n;\n \nKorintra\n-lrw\n)\n \n–\n \nCorinthians\n \n(Bible books) / Corintios (libros bíblicos)\n\nKra\n \n–\n \nmay, might\n \n/ poder, podr\ní\na\n \n(\nSee also/\n \nV\ner también:\n \nKrani\n)\n\nApia kra\n \n–\n \ncould, maybe yes or maybe no, either way\n \n/ podría, tal vez sí o tal vez no, de cualquier manera\n\nBan kra\n \n(\na/t:\n \nBankra\n)\n \n–\n \nmaybe\n \n/ tal vez\n \n(\nSee also/\n \nV\ner\n \ntambién:\n \nMebi\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nBan kra naha taimka ra, ...\n \n–\n \nMaybe at this time, ...\n \n/ Quizás en este momento\n,\n \n...\n)\n\nBan kra si\n \n–\n \nmaybe it is the case, maybe it is being the case, maybe so\n \n/ tal vez sea el\n \ncas\no\n, tal vez\n \nsiendo\n\nel caso, tal vez\n\nBan kra talia\n \n–\n \nseems like maybe, possibly\n \n/ parece que tal vez, posiblemente\n\nD\nauk\nbia\n \nkra\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nmight\n \ndo, might make, might cause\n \n/ podría hacer, podría causar\n\nKabia kra\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nmight be, might become\n \n/ podría ser, podría convertirse\n\nTak\nbia\n \nkra\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nmay\n \nhappen,\n \nmay\n \nbecome\n \n/ puede suceder, puede convertirse\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nfy15\n):\n \ndîa trabilka\n \ntakbia kra\n \n–\n \nwhat trouble may happen\n \n/ que problema puede pasar\n)\n\nWibia kra\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nmight say\n \n/ podría decir\n\nKrabu\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nKrabo\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nnance\n \n/ nancite",
